==English==
[[File:Rhizocarpon.jpg|thumb|right|Lichen growing on a rock.]]
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|līchēn||ringworm|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|λειχήν|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|lī'kən}}, {{IPA|/ˈlaɪ.kn̩/|/ˈlɪtʃ.n̩/|lang=en}},<ref>{{R:Merriam Webster Online}}</ref>
* {{audio|en-uk-lichen.ogg|Audio (UK)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|aɪkən|ɪtʃən|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|liken}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of many [[symbiotic]] [[organism]]s, being [[association]]s of [[fungi]] and [[algae]]; often found as [[white]] or [[yellow]] [[patch]]es on old [[wall]]s, etc.
#* '''1894''' — {{w|Rudyard Kipling}}, ''[[s:The Jungle Book|The Jungle Book]], Lukannon''
#*: The Beaches of Lukannon–the winter wheat so tall– <br/>The dripping, crinkled '''lichens''', and the sea-fog drenching all!
#* '''1895''' — {{w|H. G. Wells}}, ''[[s:The Time Machine|The Time Machine]]'', ch XI
#*: It was the same rich green that one sees on forest moss or on the '''lichen''' in caves: plants which like these grow in a perpetual twilight.
#* '''1915''' — {{w|John Muir}}, ''[[s:Travels in Alaska|Travels in Alaska]]'', ch V
#*: The nibble marks of the stone adze were still visible, though crusted over with scale '''lichens''' in most places.
# {{context|figurative|lang=en}} Something which [[spread]]s across something else, causing [[damage]].
#* {{RQ:Grey Riders|15}}
#*: Meanwhile, abiding a day of judgment, she fought ceaselessly to deny the bitter drops in her cup, to tear back the slow, the intangibly slow growth of a hot, corrosive '''lichen''' eating into her heart.

